<!DOCTYPE RCC>
<RCC version="1.0">
  <qresource prefix="/">
    <file>edraw.qss</file>
    <file>defaults/mech-models.json</file>
    <file>defaults/edrawlib.plb</file>
    <file>edraw.ico</file>
    <file>caret-down.svg</file>
    <file>caret-up.svg</file>
  </qresource>
  <!--
    THE LICENCE PAPERWORK, COMPILED INTO THE EXECUTABLE.

    The LGPL requires that these texts accompany the program, and the build also copies them as plain
    files into the install folder - which is where a user or a lawyer will look for them. They are ALSO
    in here, because "About Edraw -> Third-party licences" has to be able to show them, and a dialog that
    reads them off disk is a dialog that shows an empty box the first time somebody runs Edraw.exe out of
    a folder that was copied without its subdirectories. The notice is then not given, which is the one
    thing the licence actually asks of us.

    Roughly 43 KB of text in the binary. That is the price of the notice always being there.
  -->
  <qresource prefix="/licenses">
    <file alias="LGPL-3.0.txt">../licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt</file>
    <file alias="GPL-3.0.txt">../licenses/GPL-3.0.txt</file>
    <file alias="LGPL-2.1.txt">../licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt</file>
    <file alias="OCCT-LGPL-EXCEPTION-1.0.txt">../licenses/OCCT-LGPL-EXCEPTION-1.0.txt</file>
    <file alias="THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt">../THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt</file>
  </qresource>
</RCC>
